Test Case: image_from_plan
================================================================================

Step 2 Failed: AzureRM Baseline Validation

Failed Command:
terraform apply -auto-approve -input=false

Error Message:
ResourcePurchaseValidationFailed: User failed validation to purchase resources. 
Error message: 'Offer with PublisherId: 'cloudwhizsolutions', OfferId: 
'jenkins-docker-container-with-ubuntu-server' cannot be purchased due to validation errors.

The 'unknown' payment instrument(s) is not supported for offer with OfferId: 
'jenkins-docker-container-with-ubuntu-server', PlanId 'jenkins-docker-container-with-ubuntu-server-cw'.

The offer with PublisherId: 'cloudwhizsolutions', OfferId: 
'jenkins-docker-container-with-ubuntu-server' and PlanId: 
'jenkins-docker-container-with-ubuntu-server-cw' cannot be used on selected 
subscription to purchase paid marketplace offers. Please choose another subscription 
or update this one to allow purchases.

Root Cause Analysis:
This test case requires a paid marketplace image from CloudWhiz Solutions. The Azure 
subscription being used does not support purchasing paid marketplace offers - likely 
a free tier or sponsorship subscription with purchasing restrictions.

This is an environmental constraint, not a module implementation issue. The test 
cannot proceed as the baseline AzureRM configuration itself cannot be deployed.

Conclusion:
Test case is INVALID due to Azure subscription limitations preventing purchase of 
required marketplace image. This test would require either:
1. An Azure subscription with purchasing enabled and payment method configured
2. A different marketplace image that doesn't require purchase
3. Pre-acceptance of the marketplace agreement by a subscription administrator

The test cannot validate AzAPI migration as the baseline cannot be established.
